WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.520
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.680
This work is about building an AI vocoder
that is able to synthesize believable singing

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.230
from MIDI and lyrics as inputs.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.850
But first, what is a vocoder?

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.400
It works kinda like this.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.460
Fellow Scholars who are fans of Jean-Michel
Jarre's music are likely very familiar with

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.219
this effect, I've put a link to an example
song in the video description.

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:46.710
Make sure to leave a comment with your favorite
songs with vocoders so I and other Fellow

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.329
Scholars can also nerd out on them.

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:52.100
And now about the MIDI and lyrics terms.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:57.260
The lyrics part is a simple text file containing
the words that this synthesized voice should

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:03.070
sing, and the MIDI is data that describes
the pitch, length and the velocity of each

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.070
sound.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:08.590
With a little simplification, we could say
that the score is given as an input, and the

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.200
algorithm has to output the singing footage.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:16.160
We will talk about the algorithm in a moment,
but for now, let's listen to it.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:46.880
Wow.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.610
So this is a vocoder.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:54.259
This means it separates the pitch and timbre
components of the voice, therefore the waveforms

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:59.140
are not generated directly, which is a key
difference from Google DeepMind's WaveNet.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:04.939
This leads to two big advantages:
One, the generation times are quite favorable.

00:02:04.939 --> 00:02:08.060
And by favorable, I guess you're hoping for
real time.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:15.470
Well, hold on to your papers, because it is
not real time, it is 10-15 times real-time!

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:20.720
And two, this way, the algorithm will only
need a modest amount of training data to function

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:21.720
well.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.560
Here, you can see the input phonemes that
make up the syllables of the lyrics, each

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.380
typically corresponding to one note.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:35.020
This is then connected to a modified WaveNet
architecture that uses 2-by-1 dilated convolutions.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:40.670
This means that the dilation factor is doubled
in each layer, thereby introducing an exponential

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:43.240
growth in the receptive field of the model.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.320
This helps us keep the parameter count down,
which enables training on small datasets.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.519
As validation, the mean opinion scores have
been recorded, in a previous episode, we discussed

00:02:53.519 --> 00:02:59.200
that this is a number that describes how a
sound sample would pass as genuine human speech

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:00.519
or singing.

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:05.600
The test showed that this new method is well
ahead of the competition, approximately midway

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.269
between the previous works and the reference
singing footage.

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:13.900
There are plenty of other tests in the paper,
this is just one of many, so make sure to

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:14.900
have a look.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:19.970
This is one important stepping stone towards
synthesizing singing that is highly usable

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:24.180
in digital media and where generation is faster
than real time.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.930
Creating a MIDI input is a piece of cake with
a midi master keyboard, or we can even draw

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:33.120
the notes by hand in many digital audio workstation
programs.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.069
After that, writing the lyrics is as simple
as it gets and doesn't need any additional

00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:39.069
software.

00:03:39.069 --> 00:03:42.820
Tools like this are going to make this process
accessible to everyone.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:43.820
Loving it.

